    23	- **Scopes, each stated with its result:** A's missed questions and C cover a sample of 80 of the 473 articles, stratified by day (seed fixed
    24	  before the run), and are stated for those 80, not for the window; A's quality marks, B and B2 cover every question each draw opened in the
    25	  window, every last judgement by 10-05, and every statement those judgements cite (window-level).
    26	- **A, big questions:** each family lists from the 80 articles the questions worth tracking on their own; then each system's questions are
    27	  marked opened / narrower / broader / missed per matter. Counted: matters both families list, and separately matters only one lists (reported
    28	  with the disagreement, not dropped). **Covered** = opened, or narrower when the narrower question carries the matter's main outcome (each such
    29	  call written with its reason); broader and missed are not covered. Each system's opened questions are also marked worth tracking / trivia /
    30	  duplicate.
    31	- **B, judgements:** every question's last judgement by 10-05, read against the request as sent. Planted wrong judgements are built on requests
    32	  not otherwise in the packet; supported controls are confirmed by a separate reader first and any disputed control is replaced.
    33	- **B2, statements:** every statement a last judgement cites, against its own article (the passage located in the article text): date,
    34	  speaker and summary.
    35	- **C, delivery:** first, a separate fact listing: each family reads each of the 80 articles and lists every statement that bears on a covered
    36	  matter (with its passage), not only the sentences that raise a question; then code classes each listed fact per system (not extracted / no
    37	  link / linked elsewhere / delivered in the request of a judgement after it arrived), checked by hand; the undelivered ones are read against
    38	  the full judgement request ("would it change the rung?"). Controls of both kinds: known "would not" (facts already in the request, or
    39	  unrelated) and a known "would change" **group** (PRD 10's custom-chip case: a group of facts moved 9 of 9 sends off the lowest rung), read
    40	  as a group because no single-fact positive case is established.
    41	- **Denominators and empty cases:** a system that opens no question on a matter is "missed", never excluded; a system with no judgement on a
    42	  covered matter fails B for it; an empty denominator is reported as not measured, never as met.
    43	
    44	## Lines (for Alex to set; a starting proposal, not decided)
    45	
    46	| reading | proposed line, per system, in at least two of three draws | basis in the trial (leads only) |
    47	|---|---|---|
    48	| A | covers at least 4 in 5 of the matters both families list | 6–7 of 7 in the trial |
    49	| A | at most 1 in 5 of its opened questions marked trivia or duplicate by both families | clean acceptance D386: 1 of 10 |
    50	| B | at least 9 in 10 last judgements supported by both families | 7 of 9 and 10 of 12 in the trial |
    51	| B2 | at most 1 in 20 cited statements wrong in date, speaker or summary against the article | 4 of 201 flagged by both, unconfirmed |
    52	| C | no undelivered fact both families say would change a judgement | the product's purpose (PRD 10 §1) |

 succeeded in 0ms:
    13	## Readers and blinding
    14	
    15	- **Readers.** A is Codex, with memories off (D661). B is Claude, through the command line with no settings, tools, MCP or slash commands. Each
    16	  card is its own fresh session, run from an empty directory, with everything inline. Logs are checked: any command, tool or file event voids the
    17	  session.
    18	- **What a session sees.** Only the card as the page shows it to Alex: the question, the answer choices with the present answer, its reasons, the
    19	  cited statements with their passages, the complete request, the completeness sheet, and the linked articles' text, plus the fixed brief below.
    20	- **What no session sees:** the key (`~/.hivemind-keys/pilot-deck-1/`), the stored model-family marks, DESIGN.md, or which cards are planted or
    21	  repeated.
    22	- **Claude, the orchestrator,** writes no mark. Code builds every prompt from the page.
    23	
    24	## Steps (fixed)
    25	
    26	1. **Independent marks.** For each card, A and B each mark the page's own fields:
    27	   - `worth`: yes, no or cannot tell;
    28	   - `supported`: yes, no or cannot tell, answer cards only;
    29	   - per sheet fact, `bears` (yes, no or cannot tell) and `effect` (the answer, only the confidence, neither, or cannot tell);
    30	   - a short `why`.
    31	2. **Debate.** For each card where any field differs, both readers get a fresh session with the card, their own mark and reason, and the other
    32	   reader's mark and reason. Each keeps or changes each disputed field, with a reason. There are at most two rounds.
    33	3. **The council's mark.**
    34	   - **Agreed:** that value.
    35	   - **Still split after two rounds:** "cannot tell", listed as a split for Alex's spot check.
    36	4. **The tally.** The council's marks are written in the page's own format (`c<n>-worth`, `c<n>-supported`, `c<n>-why`, `c<n>-fact<i>-bears`,
    37	   `c<n>-fact<i>-effect`) and tallied by the unchanged `tally_deck.py` against the sealed key.
    38	5. **Read against D662's lines, with the time line not applicable:**
    39	   - **"Enough to design the next comparison":** both plants marked `supported = no`; the separately confirmed supported control `yes`; at least 2
    40	     of 3 repeats the same on both fields.
    41	   - **Anything unmet** is inspected for its cause.
    42	   - **Reported:** every split; agreement with each stored model family, with D661's caveat; and the sheets.
    17	## Against the lines fixed before marking
    18	
    19	| Line | Result |
    20	|---|---|
    21	| Both planted wrong answers rejected | **Yes:** cards 3 and 19, supported = no |
    22	| The confirmed supported controls accepted | **4 of 5:** cards 4, 6, 7 and 15 yes; card 5 (old v1, credit support and guarantees) split, and so is its repeat, card 11 |
    23	| Hidden repeats marked the same | **3 of 3** (cards 5/11, 6/13 and 10/16; the first pair is the same split twice) |
    24	| Missed matters | Both judged worth a question: M01 FY2027 revenue (missed by the new system) and M04 the $279B supply commitments (missed by the old) |
    25	| Completeness sheets | The 3 confirmed undelivered facts "bear" on their question, but "would change only the confidence". The 3 negative controls "do not bear" |
